"The Palace of Unbreaking is a zealous Artonan institution that preserves wordchains."
"It holds that wordchains are the original magic and keeps fragile chains alive by use."
"It restricts fragile chains to responsible users and receives their chain ledgers."
"Among Avowed only Chainers may work there; Artonan members teach once past the novice echelons."
"Its members won't bestow a chain on anyone unwilling."
"Its saying: 'We all make sacrifices for the Unbreaking.'"
"It keeps tomes of chains, some older than Artonan lingual unification, read aloud to Chainers."
"It gives Chainers' students ledgers, silver chain links and Opposite stones."
"The Grand Senate has affirmed its value; some of the strongest chains exist only through it."
"Lute Velra works there for the wizard Parethat-uur, who can force others' chains due."
"The Art'h family has a relationship with the Palace."
"The Palace has sites on all three Artonas and on a few other worlds."
"It holds exclusive summoning rights over Chainers and rarely loans them out."
"The House of the Southern Convocation is its site on Artona III."
"There, statues of Artonans hold up the edges of two giant swooping wings of bronze-like metal."
"Its parking lot is marked with patterns and logograms instead of painted spaces."
"Inside it is like an ornate conference center, full of logograms."
"A sub-level holds a hot, dim, circular tattoo room with incense and adjustable tables."
"Contract Artist Rekiss-tha tattoos every Velra's family contract there."
"The Palace leaves friendly notes in the Chainer skill list and sends new Chainers welcome gifts."
